# Documentation sync (Zyene Reviews)

## Source of truth

- Engineering hub: `docs/README.md`
- Agent system map: `codebase-analysis-docs/CODEBASE_KNOWLEDGE.md`
- Deep refs: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/API.md`, `docs/DATA_MODELS.md`, `docs/AUTHENTICATION.md`, `docs/CONFIGURATION.md`, `docs/CODING_CONVENTIONS.md`, `docs/PUBLIC_API.md`
- Standards: `AGENTS.md` (do not duplicate conflicting rules)

Growth/GEO/ops docs under `docs/` remain valid; prefer the hub above for architecture and API work.

## Before large changes

1. Consult `docs/` and `codebase-analysis-docs/CODEBASE_KNOWLEDGE.md`.
2. Prefer patterns in `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` and `docs/CODING_CONVENTIONS.md`.
3. Do not invent parallel auth, tenancy, or job systems.

## When editing code, update or flag docs

| You touch… | Update (or explicitly flag in PR) |
|------------|-----------------------------------|
| `src/app/api/**` | `docs/API.md` (and `/docs/api` UI data if public v1) |
| Auth, cookies, API keys, roles | `docs/AUTHENTICATION.md` |
| Env vars / `src/config/env.ts` | `docs/CONFIGURATION.md` + `.env.example` |
| Migrations / core tables | `docs/DATA_MODELS.md` |
| Cross-cutting architecture | `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` + `CODEBASE_KNOWLEDGE.md` |
| New reusable `lib`/`services` entry points | `docs/PUBLIC_API.md` |

If you cannot update docs in the same change, leave a short “Docs debt” note and add a bullet under **Documentation TODO** in `codebase-analysis-docs/CODEBASE_KNOWLEDGE.md`.

## Style for new documentation

- Clear Markdown: headings, tables, fenced code, Mermaid when it clarifies structure.
- Cross-link instead of copying large sections.
- Audience: engineer joining the project (or an AI agent) — precise paths and symbols.
- Mark unknown or roadmap behavior explicitly (do not invent GA status).
